Reject repeated node indices in DataLoad()'s first pass (pre-1.0 load()).

DataLoad() (src/main/saveload.c), the reader load() uses for the
numeric-magic save formats (1971-1977), restores objects in two passes.
The first, RemakeNextSEXP(), allocates each record's object and stores
it at the node index read from the file, without checking that the slot
is still free.  When two records claim one index, the second replaces
the first, and the second pass then restores the first record into the
object allocated for the second: a record declaring 200000 integers is
written into a zero-length vector, a file-controlled heap overflow.

    ==254==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x000000000001
        #0 RestoreSEXP        src/main/saveload.c:659
        #1 DataLoad           src/main/saveload.c:765

(INTEGER() of a zero-length vector is (void *) 1.)  Reject an index
that is out of range or already in use, including one taken by a
symbol.

Independent of patch 0029, which validates the forwarding tables of the
same reader; this one applies on top of it with an offset.  The upstream
PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not carried here.
Found by the load target with patch 0029 applied: oss-fuzz testcases
4545953420607488 and 5653432246272000 (2026-10-15).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #382, filed 2026-10-16.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/saveload.c
+++ b/src/main/saveload.c
@@ -509,6 +509,13 @@
     SEXP s = R_NilValue;	/* -Wall */
 
     idx = m->InInteger(fp, d);
+    if (idx >= (unsigned int) node->NTotal)
+	error(_("corrupt data file: node index out of range"));
+    /* the second pass restores each record into the node at its index:
+       a repeated index would have it write one record's contents into
+       an object allocated, with a different length, from another */
+    if (VECTOR_ELT(node->NewAddress, idx) != R_NilValue)
+	error(_("corrupt data file: duplicate node index"));
     type = FixupType(m->InInteger(fp, d), version);
 
     /* skip over OBJECT, LEVELS, and ATTRIB */
